="preview-time">10:42</div><div class="preview-date">Thursday · August 6</div><div class="preview-next">Next · Midday pause · 12:32 PM</div></div></div><div class="preview-day"><div class="preview-rail"><span></span><b></b></div><div class="preview-labels"><span>8:30</span><span>Day unfold · 61%</span><span>4:30</span></div></div><div class="preview-rhythm"><span>Fajr<strong>5:17</strong></span><span>Dhuhr<strong>1:23</strong></span><span class="next">Asr<strong>5:18</strong></span><span>Maghrib<strong>8:35</strong></span><span>Isha<strong>10:08</strong></span></div><div class="preview-fold"><div><small>Daybook</small><br><strong>Notes and today remain visible</strong></div><div class="preview-tabs"><i>Notes</i><i>Day</i><i>Now</i></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section alt" id="inside"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">The best ideas, brought into one place</div><h2>One product—not a stack of old versions.</h2></div><p>Pacefold now has one public surface and one current release gate. The proven local engine remains underneath for continuity, while obsolete visual layers and historical product concepts no longer define the experience.</p></div><div class="feature-grid">
<article class="feature wide"><span class="feature-tag">Clock + Day Unfold</span><h3>See the moment and the shape of the day.</h3><p>The analog and digital clock, moving workday sun, progress arc and upcoming moments form one instrument. The clock remains home; every other page returns through it.</p><div class="mini-actions"><span class="on">Analog + digital</span><span>Second hand</span><span>Moving day sun</span><span>Workday markers</span></div></article>
<article class="feature"><span class="feature-tag">Quiet actions</span><h3>Log the small things in one tap.</h3><p>Hydration, preparation timer, rest, meals, eye resets and movement use explicit states and leave an honest local record.</p></article>
<article class="feature"><span class="feature-tag">Daybook</span><h3>The notebook stays in the room.</h3><p>A visible lower fold shows today, recent notes and quick paths to Notes, Worklog, Now and Settings—without modal clutter.</p></article>
<article class="feature"><span class="feature-tag">Personal rhythm</span><h3>Faith-aware when useful. Neutral when not.</h3><p>Use location-aware Islamic prayer times, everyday reset moments, mindfulness, another editable preset or a completely custom schedule.</p></article>
<article class="feature"><span class="feature-tag">Private by design</span><h3>Your workday is not an analytics product.</h3><p>No account, advertising or behavioural tracking. Notes and logs stay in the browser, with a backup you can download and keep.</p></article>
<article class="feature wide"><span class="feature-tag">Installable</span><h3>Feels like a small desktop instrument.</h3><p>Install Pacefold from Edge or Chrome for a focused window, offline shell and taskbar cues. It still works as a normal website when installation is unavailable.</p><div class="mini-actions"><span class="on">Edge</span><span>Chrome</span><span>Windows PWA</span><span>Mobile browser</span><span>Offline shell</span></div></article>
</div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Four principles</div><h2>Calm is a behaviour, not decoration.</h2></div><p>The interface is designed around fewer owners, fewer hidden states and fewer reasons to reopen settings. It remembers what you chose and keeps the current action obvious.</p></div><div class="principles"><article class="principle"><b>01</b><strong>Clock first</strong><p>The central instrument is always the reliable home state.</p></article><article class="principle"><b>02</b><strong>Visible state</strong><p>Start, stop, waiting and logged are expressed directly.</p></article><article class="principle"><b>03</b><strong>Local continuity</strong><p>Updates preserve notes, preferences and workday records.</p></article><article class="principle"><b>04</b><strong>Honest boundaries</strong><p>Browser and Windows limitations are stated instead of simulated.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section alt"><div class="wrap launch"><div><div class="eyebrow">Ready now</div><h2>Open the day instrument.</h2><p>Start immediately, or take one minute to choose your work hours, rhythm profile, timer and care cadence.</p></div><div class="launch-actions"><a class="button primary" href="./app/">Open Pacefold</a><a class="button" href="./app/?setup=1">Guided setup</a><button class="button" type="button" data-install>Install Pacefold</button></div></div></section>
</main>
<footer class="wrap site-footer"><span>Pacefold ${RELEASE} · Your day, quietly kept.</span><nav><a href="./privacy.html">Privacy</a><a href="./app/">App</a><a href="https://github.com/rbt4/pacefold">GitHub</a></nav></footer>
<div class="toast" id="siteToast" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
